</code></pre></div></div></div></div><div class="code-block-fade-overlay print:hidden" data-fade-overlay="true" aria-hidden="true" style="--fade-color-light:#ffffff;--fade-color-dark:#0B0C0E"></div></div>
<span data-as="p"><code>token0Mint</code> / <code>token1Mint</code> are <strong>sorted by public-key byte order</strong> (token0 &lt; token1) before hashing. Getting this wrong yields a valid PDA for a non-existent pool.</span>
<span data-as="p">The equivalent CLMM seeds follow the same style; see <a class="link" href="/products/clmm/accounts"><code>products/clmm/accounts</code></a>.</span>
