 mainnet-beta and devnet. Every other page links here instead of hardcoding addresses.\",\"href\":\"/reference/program-addresses\"},{\"title\":\"Error codes\",\"description\":\"Anchor error enums for every Raydium on-chain program, with cause and recommended UX message.\",\"href\":\"/reference/error-codes\"},{\"title\":\"Fee comparison\",\"description\":\"Side-by-side fee matrix across all Raydium products — swap fees, protocol shares, creation costs, and how Token-2022 transfer fees stack on top. A single-page lookup for expected costs.\",\"href\":\"/reference/fee-comparison\"},{\"title\":\"Token-2022 support matrix\",\"description\":\"Which Raydium programs support Token-2022, the explicit extension allow-list each program enforces at pool creation, and the bypass paths (static mint whitelist, per-mint registry, Superstate detection) that admit otherwise-rejected mints.\",\"href\":\"/reference/token-2022-support\"},{\"title\":\"Glossary\",\"description\":\"Definitions of terms used throughout Raydium's documentation. Each entry has a one-line definition and a pointer to the page where the term is explained in depth.\",\"href\":\"/reference/glossary\"},{\"group\":\"Changelog\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Changelog\",\"sidebarTitle\":\"Overview\",\"description\":\"Timeline index of updates to this documentation set. Each release links to its own page detailing which chapters changed, why, and when the content was verified against on-chain state and the program source.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"2026-08-31 — LaunchLab: platform curve rules replace the curve-parameter whitelist\",\"description\":\"Launch-parameter restrictions move from PlatformConfig.curve_params into per-config PlatformCurveRule accounts with (field, op, value) constraints, value bands, ORed check groups, and a delegated manager wallet. PlatformConfig keeps its 944-byte size; the legacy field and its two instructions are removed, and seven error codes are appended.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-08-31-launchlab-platform-curve-rules\"},{\"title\":\"2026-08-27 — LaunchLab: platform holds the withdraw-withheld authority from mint creation\",\"description\":\"InitializeWithToken2022 now writes PlatformConfig.transfer_fee_extension_auth into the new base mint's withdraw_withheld_authority instead of the launch authority PDA, and MigrateToCpswap only reassigns that authority when the PDA still holds it. No account layout, instruction, or error change.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-08-27-launchlab-token2022-withheld-authority\"},{\"title\":\"2026-08-26 — LaunchLab: platform fee rate cap raised to 500 bps\",\"description\":\"The platform fee_rate ceiling moves to 500 bps on both the create and the update path. CreatePlatformConfig was capped at 100 bps and UpdatePlatformConfig at 250 bps; both are now 50000. No account layout, instruction, or error change.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-08-26-launchlab-platform-fee-rate-cap\"},{\"title\":\"2026-08-24 — LaunchLab: Token-2022 quote mints\",\"description\":\"LaunchLab accepts Token-2022 quote mints across config, pool creation, swaps, fee claims, and CPMM migration. Swap slippage bounds now price the quote-side transfer fee, PoolState.token_program_flag bit1 becomes meaningful, and MigrateToCpswap renames its two token-program accounts.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-08-24-launchlab-token2022-quote-mint\"},{\"title\":\"2026-08-17 — LaunchLab: CPMM-only launches and platform config controls\",\"description\":\"LaunchLab makes CPMM mandatory for new launches, consolidates locked LP under the platform, replaces global platform authorization with platform-managed config allowlists, and updates CPMM migration accounts.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-08-17-launchlab-cpmm-only-platform-config\"},{\"title\":\"2026-08-17 — CLMM: restricted-issuer position NFT freezing\",\"description\":\"CLMM conditionally freezes a new position NFT account only when a V2 open path finds an underlying mint whose freeze authority matches the restricted-issuer list.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-08-17-clmm-restricted-position-nft-freeze\"},{\"title\":\"2026-08-17 — CPMM: permissionless creator-fee collection\",\"description\":\"CPMM adds a destination-constrained instruction that lets any payer sweep creator fees to the pool creator's canonical ATAs, and delegates Permission PDA creation without delegating revocation.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-08-17-cpmm-permissionless-creator-fee-collection\"},{\"title\":\"2026-07-30 — CLMM: permissioned multi-pools and limit-order frozen-account guard\",\"description\":\"Two CLMM program updates: CreatePermissionedPool lets a whitelisted authority create multiple pools per pair via a seed_index folded into the pool PDA, and OpenLimitOrder now takes the output-side accounts to reject orders with a frozen input or output token account.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-07-30-clmm-permissioned-pools\"},{\"title\":\"2026-07-22 — AMM v4: remove OpenBook / Serum dependency\",\"description\":\"AMM v4 removes its dormant OpenBook/Serum dependency, CPIs, and market-making instructions: v1 Swap/Deposit/Withdraw stay compatible, WithdrawPnl and SetParams are hard-breaking, and several instructions are no longer callable.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-07-22-amm-v4-openbook-removal\"},{\"title\":\"2026-06-22 — Stable AMM: remove dead OpenBook (market) code\",\"description\":\"Stable AMM removes its dormant OpenBook market-making accounts and code: smaller Swap/Deposit/Withdraw layouts, a hard-breaking WithdrawPnl change, and a simplified pool-asset formula.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-06-22-stable-amm-openbook-cleanup\"},{\"title\":\"2026-05-18 — CLMM: limit orders, single-sided fee, dynamic fee\",\"description\":\"Three opt-in, backwards-compatible CLMM capabilities: first-class limit orders, single-sided fee collection, and a volatility-tracking dynamic fee — plus the PoolState reshape and new error codes.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-05-18-clmm-limit-orders\"},{\"title\":\"2026-04-26 — Initial publication\",\"description\":\"First public release of the Raydium documentation set.\",\"href\":\"/reference/changelog/2026-04-26-initial-publication\"}]}]},{\"group\":\"Resources\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Resources\",\"description\":\"Brand assets, community-built tools, and licensing for Raydium's code, SDK, and documentation.\",\"href\":\"/resources/index\"},{\"title\":\"Brand kit\",\"description\":\"Logos, colors, typography, and usage rules for representing Raydium in press, integrations, partner content, and dashboards.\",\"href\":\"/resources/brand-kit\"},{\"title\":\"Community tools\",\"description\":\"Third-party SDKs, dashboards, bots, and analytics platforms that integrate with Raydium — plus how to submit your own tool for inclusion.\",\"href\":\"/resources/community-tools\"},{\"title\":\"License\",\"description\":\"License terms for Raydium's on-chain programs, the TypeScript SDK, and this documentation. Trademark notes for the Raydium name and logo.\",\"href\":\"/resources/license\"}]}]}]},{\"language\":\"zh\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"zh\",\"href\":\"/zh/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"zh-Hant\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"zh-Hant\",\"href\":\"/zh-Hant/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"ja\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"ja\",\"href\":\"/ja/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"ko\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"ko\",\"href\":\"/ko/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"ru\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"ru\",\"href\":\"/ru/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"es\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"es\",\"href\":\"/es/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"de\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"de\",\"href\":\"/de/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"fr\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"fr\",\"href\":\"/fr/reference/program-addresses\"}]},{\"language\":\"pt\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"pt\",\"